    "id": "333ad5faa55ba99d8f9d3d8f",
    "path": "datafusion_tracing::rule_instrumentation::SingleSpanTreeTraverser",
    "name": "SingleSpanTreeTraverser",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "datafusion-tracing",
    "version": "55.0.0",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct SingleSpanTreeTraverser<'a>",
    "docs": "Applies an optimizer rule across the tree manually, keeping all work under a single span.\n\nWhen a rule specifies `apply_order()` as `Some(TopDown)` or `Some(BottomUp)`, the optimizer\nframework would normally handle tree traversal, calling the rule's `rewrite` method on each\nnode. This would result in one span per node if we simply wrapped the inner rule.\n\nInstead, `SingleSpanTreeTraverser` takes over tree traversal so that the entire rule\napplication (across all nodes) is consolidated under a single tracing span. This gives\ncleaner traces that show one span per rule rather than one span per (rule × node) combination.",
    "span": {
      "filename": "src/rule_instrumentation.rs",
